From 244d7776b02a01605869c236d9bbccfd0ed44eb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 00:35:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: arm_scmi: mailbox: fix ACPI match driver_data type
 confusion (NCZ 0085)

CIXHA006 (the SCMI mailbox transport ACPI match, added by patch 0001)
set .driver_data = (kernel_ulong_t)&scmi_mailbox_desc. scmi_mailbox_desc
is a struct scmi_desc (ops/timeouts/msg sizes) -- it is already wired
into the transport correctly via DEFINE_SCMI_TRANSPORT_DRIVER own __desc
macro parameter (memcpy-d into strans.desc). It has nothing to do with
device_get_match_data().

In the current (v7.2-era) common.h, device_get_match_data() is used for
a *different*, newer purpose: an optional struct scmi_transport_handle *
carrying two function pointers (supplier_get/supplier_put), added to
support transports whose supplier device is not tracked by firmware
description. The macro-generated probe does:

    strans.th = device_get_match_data(dev);
    if (strans.th) {
        supplier = strans.th->supplier_get(strans.th);

With driver_data pointing at scmi_mailbox_desc instead of a real
scmi_transport_handle, this calls a function pointer read out of the
wrong struct entirely -- an address inside scmi_mailbox_desc that
happens to not be executable memory. Confirmed on real Sky1 hardware
(.66) with kernel 7.2.0-rc1-ncz:

  Unable to handle kernel execute from non-executable memory at
  virtual address ffff000001922240
  pc : scmi_mailbox_probe+0x5c/0x1b8
  lr : scmi_mailbox_probe+0x5c/0x1b8
  ...
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Attempted to kill init!

This is a 6.6-era CIX patch (0001) never updated for the newer
scmi_transport_handle mechanism -- confirmed absent entirely from the
7.1-line arm_scmi/common.h (grep for scmi_transport_handle/supplier_get
there returns nothing), so the same driver_data value was harmless
there and only became live once 7.2 picked up the mainline refactor.
The OF match entry (arm,scmi) never set driver_data at all -- this
just brings the ACPI entry in line with it.

Fix: drop the driver_data assignment. strans.th then stays NULL and
the if (strans.th) guard correctly skips the supplier_get call, matching
DT-boot behavior.

This is the SCMI mailbox transport, the lowest-level shared plumbing
under clk-scmi (0003/0075), pmdomain-scmi (0077/0082), and panthor
SCMI rate-limiting (0084) -- until this crash is fixed nothing
downstream of SCMI (including NPU/VPU DKMS ACPI dependencies) is
even reachable on 7.2.
---
 drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/transports/mailbox.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/transports/mailbox.c b/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/transports/mailbox.c
index 8ad5fcae12df..5a85b99a5eb3 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/transports/mailbox.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/transports/mailbox.c
@@ -383,7 +383,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id scmi_of_match[] = {
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, scmi_of_match);
 
 static const struct acpi_device_id scmi_acpi_match[] = {
-	{ .id = "CIXHA006", .driver_data = (kernel_ulong_t)&scmi_mailbox_desc },
+	{ .id = "CIXHA006" },
 	{ /* Sentinel */ },
 };
 
